---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<p>
		Most cyberattacks do not start with advanced malware or highly skilled hackers. They start
		with people.
	</p>

	<p>
		A click on a fake link. A response to a scam text message. A password that was reused on
		multiple websites. Cybercriminals know that people are often the easiest way into an
		account, device, or network.
	</p>

	<p>
		Cybersecurity awareness is one of the best defenses against these attacks. The more you
		understand how scams and online threats work, the easier they are to spot and avoid.
	</p>

	<p>That is why HatoSec exists.</p>

	<p>
		HatoSec was created to make cybersecurity awareness easy to understand for everyone,
		regardless of age or technical background. Here you will find practical articles that
		break down real-world threats, scams, and security concepts into simple, useful information.
	</p>

	<p>Every article follows the HATO method:</p>

	<p>
		<strong>Heads Up</strong> — Why this matters and who it affects.<br />
		<strong>At a Glance</strong> — A quick summary of the threat.<br />
		<strong>The Threat</strong> — How the attack works and why it succeeds.<br />
		<strong>Outsmart It</strong> — Practical steps you can take to stay safe.
	</p>

	<p>
		The goal is not to overwhelm you with technical jargon. The goal is to help you recognize
		threats, make informed decisions, and build safer online habits.
	</p>

	<p>
		HatoSec is completely free. There are no advertisements, sponsored posts, affiliate links,
		subscriptions, or premium content. I do not sell products or services. This website exists
		for one reason: to help people stay safe online.
	</p>

	<p>
		The internet is not getting any safer, but a little knowledge can go a long way.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>Stay aware. Stay informed. Stay secure.</strong>
	</p>
</Layout>
